# Subagent Policy (mandatory before any work)

Read and obey this before starting any task in ProjectFlow.

## Allowed — use these

Launch Cursor **Auto** and **Composer** subagents when useful, especially for large
programs that request maximum safe parallelism.

- **Auto** — allowed and expected for parallel feature/review/audit work
- **Composer** — allowed

When the user or an approved program asks for multi-agent execution, the Lead
**must** fill available Auto/Composer slots with independent tasks rather than
serializing everything in one agent.

## Forbidden — only this class

The ban is on **subagent APIs / external agent runners**, not on Auto itself.

Do **not**:

- use or invoke **subagent APIs**
- request approval to enable/use subagent APIs
- call external agent APIs, SDK agent runners, or equivalent subagent API surfaces
- work around the ban with Cursor SDK / REST `/v1/agents` / similar automation APIs

## Other Cursor Task subagent types

Do not launch non-Auto/Composer Task types (for example explore-only wrappers,
bugbot, security-review APIs, or other specialized Task `subagent_type` values)
unless the user explicitly overrides this rule for that session.

If a requested capability seems to require a forbidden API rather than a normal
Auto/Composer subagent — **stop and ask the user**.

## Lead / Integrator duties when using Auto

- Lead owns shared architecture, migration numbering, financial contracts, tenancy
- Avoid multiple agents editing the same shared files at once
- Agents must not invent overlapping schema or weaken tests
- Integrate results; fix BLOCKER/HIGH/MEDIUM before closing a wave
